codemap 9
tour feature-add-step
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note Add code to the tour being read, from wherever it is shown. The reader reaches for it to turn code already on screen into a step without switching to the CLI (the human builds tours by hand). The target strip, on the Tours list, on Symbols, on Source and on the Graph tab, names the one add for what is in front of you. On the Source tab with lines selected it adds those lines. Otherwise it adds the focused symbol, and it offers nothing when that symbol is already the selected whole-symbol step. The palette entry 'add step' does the same thing. The hover '+ step' controls stay. In the Source view, select lines (click a line, or press and drag over several) and press the target strip's add button, which names them ('add lines 12-20 as a step'); the Source toolbar holds no second add for the same lines. On a Symbols row or a References caller or callee row, press '+ step', shown while the row is hovered, to add that symbol whole; 'add step' under the References heading adds the selected symbol. On an off-tour graph node, '+ step' adds its symbol. The step is authored by the human and hangs under the target (see feature-choose-target), except a graph node revealed as a callee of a step, which hangs under that step. The same lines under the same parent again is refused with the step's number; adding moves neither the selection nor the target, so the next add lands beside this one. The status names the new step's number and parent.

